# What NOT to send to the daemon when this repository is a build context.
#
# There is one such build: docker/Dockerfile.bootstrap, which reads pom.xml, mvnw, .mvn/ and
# src/main/. Everything named here is either large, private to a run, or host-built and unusable in
# the image — and the context is packed and sent on every rebuild, so a directory left in it is
# paid for every time.
#
# .claude/ is the loud one: it holds git worktrees, which are whole second checkouts of this
# repository. Without this line the context carries the repository several times over.
.claude/
.git/
target/
target-ide/

# A run's own files. .env holds this machine's answers, the clones are a platform's worth of
# source, and the log grows to megabytes.
.env
.qits-bootstrap-src/
.qits-bootstrap/
qits-bootstrap-cli.log
